{
  "comment": "@spec AUTOMATED-REMEDIATION-12 @spec AUTOMATED-REMEDIATION-17 @spec AUTOMATED-REMEDIATION-26. The declared-read predicate (maintainer ruling 2026-10-07: one RFC 6901 JSON pointer and a closed comparator set, not an expression language), frozen across three images: the runner's pointer extraction (the `read` phase answers only the sample, never the result), the worker's sample report to the API, and the API's evaluator. `extractions`: given a read tool's `structured` content (null when the tool returned none) and `is_error`, the runner yields `sample`, one of `sample_kinds`, with `value` the pointed JSON scalar for `value` and null otherwise. A scalar whose compact JSON text (ensure_ascii false) exceeds `value_max_chars` code points is `value_too_long`. `successful` names the kinds a verifier counts as a sample taken (AUTOMATED-REMEDIATION-18); the others are unsuccessful samples, never refusals. `invalid_pointers` are refused at policy write (policy_document_invalid) and by the runner (invalid_request, without dialing). `sample_report` is the worker's body for `POST /action-executions/{id}/samples`: the fence, the zero-based sample `index`, and the sample and value exactly as the runner answered. `evaluations`: the API evaluator's `result` (one of `results`) for a declared `comparator` and `value` (no `value` for `absent`) against a reported sample. Ordering comparators apply only when both sides are JSON numbers (booleans are not numbers); otherwise eq, ne and in compare type and value exactly, and an ordering comparator is unsatisfied. Read by runner/tests/test_runner_execute_vector.py (the extraction cases and invalid pointers, through the real `read` phase), apps/worker/tests/test_remediation_predicate_vector.py and apps/api/tests/test_remediation_predicate_vector.py, each of which rejects an unknown key.",
